  "solution": {
    "approach": "Find minimum base B such that the given number string is valid in base B.",
    "timeComplexity": "O(D)",
    "spaceComplexity": "O(1)",
    "code": {
      "C": "#include <stdio.h>\nint main() {\n    char s[1005]; if (scanf(\"%s\", s) != 1) return 0;\n    int max_d = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; s[i]; i++) if (s[i] - '0' > max_d) max_d = s[i] - '0';\n    printf(\"%d\\n\", max_d + 1);\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "C++": "#include <iostream>\n#include <string>\nusing namespace std;\nint main() {\n    string s; if (!(cin >> s)) return 0;\n    int max_d = 0;\n    for (char c : s) if (c - '0' > max_d) max_d = c - '0';\n    cout << (max_d + 1) << \"\\n\";\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "Java": "import java.util.Scanner;\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        if (sc.hasNext()) {\n            String s = sc.next();\n            int maxD = 0;\n            for (char c : s.toCharArray()) if (c - '0' > maxD) maxD = c - '0';\n            System.out.println(maxD + 1);\n        }\n    }\n}\n",
      "Python3": "import sys\ndef main():\n    toks = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if toks: print(max(int(c) for c in toks[0]) + 1)\nif __name__ == \"__main__\": main()\n",
      "JavaScript": "const fs = require(\"fs\");\nfunction main() {\n    const toks = fs.readFileSync(0, \"utf-8\").trim().split(/\\s+/);\n    if (toks && toks[0]) {\n        let m = 0;\n        for (const c of toks[0]) {\n            const d = parseInt(c, 10);\n            if (d > m) m = d;\n        }\n        console.log(m + 1);\n    }\n}\nmain();\n"
    },
    "notes": "Ensure standard I/O format handling.",
    "editorial": "The minimum valid base is max(digits) + 1."
  },
